
  Needs .env (read by process.env)

  perplexed/.env
  PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=
  ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
  Read by main.ts:107-108. Also configurable in plugin settings UI.

  file-transporter/.env
  GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
  GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
  GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/oauth2callback   # optional
  Read by src/utils/SimpleGoogleAuth.ts:18-20.

  image-gin/.env (already exists)
  RECRAFT_API_KEY=
  RECRAFT_STYLE_ID=
  Plus, if you use the other providers, set them in data.json settings UI: magnific.apiKey,
  ideogram.apiKey.

  grab-reference/.env (this is a containerized service, not a vault plugin — it has Docker/Postgres)
  YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
  GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY=
  DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@postgres:5432/citation_db

  Configured in Obsidian settings UI → persisted to data.json

  cite-wide → jinaApiKey (Jina AI — https://jina.ai)
  plunk-it → plunkApiToken (from https://app.useplunk.com/settings/api-keys)
  filestarter → apiKey (OpenGraph API — likely opengraph.io)
  obsidian-git → username + password/PAT (stored in Obsidian's localStorage, not data.json; entered
  via modal on first push)

  No keys needed

  lmstud-yo — talks to local LM Studio at http://localhost:1234 (already in data.json)

  ---
  Summary of what to create:
  - perplexed/.env — Perplexity + Anthropic
  - file-transporter/.env — Google OAuth client ID + secret
  - image-gin/.env already exists; just fill in Recraft key
  - grab-reference/.env — YouTube + Google Books (only if you run that service)